AnthropicUsage.description:
Anthropic ``usage`` — input/output token counts plus the cache
fields (always 0 here — the gated pipeline has no prompt cache;
reporting zeros is the honest contract).

OpenAIChatResponse.description:
POST /v1/chat/completions 200 body — the `chat.completion`
envelope. `system_fingerprint` carries the serving backend name;
`usage` is null when the provider didn't report token counts.

post.description:
Cooperative cancel — the worker checks the flag between items;
an in-flight item finishes, then the batch ends with ``canceled``
rows for the unprocessed tail.
